    "A token is a full credential: on every endpoint it stands in for the username and password, so the Apple TV app and scripts can hold their own secret instead of your password. Certificate download and every delete action are always locked — they need the password, and when a token is set they need that token too, which also locks the browser's certificate list. Changing any of these restarts the server." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A token is a full credential: on every endpoint it stands in for the username and password, so the Apple TV app and scripts can hold their own secret instead of your password. Certificate download and every delete action are always locked — they need the password, and when a token is set they need that token too, which also locks the browser's certificate list. Changing any of these restarts the server."
          }
        }
      }
    },
